;;-*-Lisp-*-
(in-package goal)

;; jak-hd.gc — HD character ANIMATION-RETARGET companions.
;; Grecharged-hd-models3 (M1: Jak) + Grecharged-hd-models4 (M2: Daxter/Keira/Samos + per-actor coverage).
;;
;; DESIGN (owner-chosen anim-retarget, NOT re-rig). A stock DRIVER process (the player *target*, the
;; sidekick, a village NPC, a cutscene/logo actor) keeps playing jak1's animations and owns the
;; hardcoded joint-node attach refs. We keep each HD model's OWN skeleton + authored weights, load it
;; as its own skelgroup, and run a COMPANION process `jak-hd` per driver INSTANCE that, every frame
;; AFTER the driver, fills the HD skeleton's world bone matrices from the driver's animated bones via
;; a name-mapped retarget (k->e table). The stock skinning path then skins the HD mesh.
;;
;; M4 REPLACEMENT TABLE (owner roadmap 2026-08-03): any process-drawable whose merc name matches a
;; table entry gets its own companion — "le modèle choisi PARTOUT" (gameplay, cutscenes, ND logo):
;;     eichar-lod0    -> jak-hd    (jak2 jakone-highres,  75 joints)  [M1]
;;     sidekick-lod0  -> dax-hd    (jak3 daxter-highres,  62 joints, NO-pants cinematic)
;;     assistant-lod0 -> keira-hd  (jak2 keira-highres,   95 joints, first-cutscene LINTCSTB)
;;     sage-lod0      -> samos-hd  (jak3 samos-highres,   80 joints)
;;
;; M5 PER-CHARACTER LOOK (Grecharged-hd-models5): the table above is no longer a 1:1 name->model
;; map. A driver name now yields a CHARACTER (0 jak, 1 daxter, 2 keira, 3 samos) and that
;; character's LOOK setting (hd-look-jak/-daxter/-keira/-samos in *pc-settings*) picks WHICH of the
;; eleven ENTRIES it wears: 0..3 are the jak1-look HD models (LOOK "HD", the M1/M2 behaviour), 4..10
;; are the bonus donors (jak2-hd, jak3-hd, daxp-hd, keira3-hd, ysamos-hd, jakm-hd, jakp-hd). LOOK 0 = ORIGINAL means
;; NO companion at all — the stock jak1 mesh, unsuppressed. Changing a look at runtime despawns the
;; stale companion (reconcile pass in maybe-spawn-jak-hd!) and the next scan spawns the new one.
;;
;; PER-ACTOR COVERAGE (M4 carry-over fix; ND-logo invisible Jak). The driver's own low-poly draw is
;; suppressed RENDERER-side, but ONLY per actor: every pc-merc packet carries its owner pid
;; (bones.gc), each companion registers (pc-hd-cover! companion-pid driver-pid) at spawn and
;; unregisters at despawn, and Merc2 drops a stock packet ONLY while THAT pid's companion is actively
;; submitting with its HD model found. An actor no companion covers (asset missing, spawn failed)
;; always keeps its stock draw — suppression without a replacement can never recur. Never suppress
;; via skip-bones on *target*: the sidekick's :post copies that status wholesale, which swallowed
;; Daxter (M1 builds 10-12).
;;
;; RETARGET MATH — proven offline to machine precision (retarget_fill_table.py PROOF A err 8.9e-16).
;; For HD joint k mapped to driver joint e = k2e[k], in COLUMN convention:
;;     bones_hd[k].transform = M_anim(e) . IBM_driver(e) . inverse(IBM_hd[k])
;; STORAGE ORDER WARNING: the engine is ROW-VECTOR ((matrix*! d a b) = a.b, a applied FIRST; the
;; palette asm computes v . IBM_hd . bones_hd) — so as STORED row products this must be built as
;;     bones_hd[k] = inverse(IBM_hd[k]) . IBM_driver(e) . M_anim(e)     <- fill-jak-hd-bones!
;; Building it in the column order verbatim produces the build10 exploded-spikes carnage.
;; where M_anim(e)   = (-> drv  draw skeleton bones (+ e 1) transform)   ; driver animated world
;;       IBM_driver  = (-> drv  draw jgeo    data   e     bind-pose)     ; driver inverse bind
;;       IBM_hd[k]   = (-> self draw jgeo    data   k     bind-pose)     ; HD inverse bind
;; The stock new-bones-mtx-calc-asm then post-multiplies IBM_hd[k] -> the proven skin palette.
;; Unmapped joints (e = #xff) follow the driver's root joint (align, e=0) — a model-space matrix in
;; a world-space bone slot anchors parts at world origin (the build10 'giant blade spike').
;;
;; INDEX SPACES (align off-by-one, verified): the k->e table keys AND values are GAME joint numbers
;; (align = 0 on both sides — prep_hd_actor_glb.py drops rip-align then build_actor re-prepends align,
;; so game-joint-index == rip-skin-index). Skeleton node = joint-index + 1 (node 0 unused, node 1 =
;; align). Hence read driver at (+ e 1), write HD at (+ k 1).
;;
;; ENGINE<->PC BOUNDARY: this is a PC file. It is spawned/ticked ONLY from PC context (a forward-
;; declared call inside (update *pc-settings*)), never from an engine file — an engine->PC call would
;; be an unbound fn-ptr = SIGILL (the class that crashed menu V3).
;;
;; IP: the HD art-groups (<char>-ag.go) are Naughty-Dog-derived and live ONLY in the external asset
;; pack, loaded from disk at runtime. Never baked into the binary/custom pack. Gated behind the
;; FLAG_HD_MODELS build flag + the recharged-enhanced-models? runtime setting.

(#when FLAG_HD_MODELS

;; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; per-actor coverage registry (Merc2.cpp, registered in jak1/kmachine.cpp)
;; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
(define-extern pc-hd-cover! (function int int none))
(define-extern pc-hd-uncover! (function int none))

;; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; retarget tables v2: per character, FOUR parallel arrays (mirrors of *-k2e.gc-snippet):
;;   *<c>->driver-joint*  HD game joint k -> driver game joint e (255 = no counterpart)
;;   *<c>-mode*           0 = world-delta, 1 = local-delta mapped, 2 = local-delta glue,
;;                        3 = orient-copy (cycle 3: mapped joint with mismatched local bind frame)
;;   *<c>-hd-parent*      HD rig parent joint index (255 = root/none), always < k for modes 1/2
;;   *<c>-drv-parent*     driver rig parent of the mapped driver joint (255 = n/a)
;; generated by scripts/shell/retarget_fill_table.py (FACE-FINGER-GATE enforced) — do not hand-edit.
;; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
